{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3074","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3074","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3074\",\"parent_revision\":\"bb2bae30818e8366411698932ebc0bb386677c89b8c50c05911cf2991190a462\",\"root_revision\":\"bb2bae30818e8366411698932ebc0bb386677c89b8c50c05911cf2991190a462\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Decision Needed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRecorded as open question 3 in `docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`, with no backlog\\ntracking until now.\\n\\nR2 requires pagination when a response would exceed budget. Undecided: does the calling agent\\nget a parameter to request a smaller (or larger, up to the harness cap) page than the\\nconfigured default, or is page size fixed to whatever the engine's budget constant is set to?\\n\\nArguments live on both sides and are not resolved here \u2014 this issue exists to make the decision\\ntrackable, not to make it:\\n\\n- Caller control gives an agent facing tight remaining context a way to ask for less.\\n- No caller control keeps every response predictably sized and simplifies the R8 identity/cache\\n  contract (fewer distinct page shapes to key against).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why This Blocks Work\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#3059 (engine-served navigation) and #3062 (content-identity addressing) both define the page\\nrequest/response contract. Building either without this decision risks a parameter shape that\\nhas to change again once decided.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Resolution\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nUpdate `docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`'s open-questions section to remove item 3\\nonce decided, and record the chosen answer directly in R2 or R5.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2566df16d0b3cc2743fe1ec5a7cee1523d9317564787ad43dae6d4702ab8dd06\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvcF3A\"}"}